{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.QSubstrate","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.LightNucleus","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.WitnessR5Full","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Helium3Witness","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DeuteronWitness","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TritiumWitness","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.MassFormulaCategorical"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMassMeV_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMassMeV_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L115-L119","doc":"The MeV mass prediction is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L109-L113","doc":"The categorical mass prediction is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMassMeV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMassMeV","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L105-L107","doc":"**MeV-converted mass prediction**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.nucleusMass","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L100-L103","doc":"**Categorical mass prediction** for nucleus `n`, using the\nR5-full witness's `rho_star` and the placeholder T_w. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.placeholder_T_w","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.placeholder_T_w","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**Placeholder T_w element** for nucleus `n` — currently the\nzero element of `HeckeElement n.n₀`. Real values come from\n`braidWordEval n.n₀ <bindingKWord n>` once the algebra\nevaluation map is concretely defined.\n\nThe placeholder makes the mass formula type-check and gives\na (vacuous, zero-valued) prediction; downstream theorems\nwill substitute real T_w values. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.m_e_cat_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.m_e_cat_pos","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**Theorem** (was previously an axiom; discharged 2026-06-07).\nPositivity of `m_e_cat` follows from the placeholder literal\nbeing positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.m_e_cat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PerNucleusMassDerivation.m_e_cat","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PerNucleusMassDerivation.lean#L60-L79","doc":"**Cat-units electron mass** placeholder.  Real value comes\nfrom the proton chain's `m_e_Hecke ≈ 0.0007783` (per\n`derivation_chain.M_HECKE_PIPELINE_AT_Q0`).\n\n**`def` form (was previously an `axiom`).**  Discharged\n2026-06-07 by binding to the witness's approximate value\n`0.0007783`. The axiom previously committed to no value\n(only existence) and let downstream proofs use it\nopaquely; the only theorem that depended on `m_e_cat`\nsemantically was `m_e_cat_pos`, which now follows by\n`norm_num` from the literal. Other consumers\n(`nucleusMass`, `nucleusMassMeV`) treat `m_e_cat` as a\nscalar and do not care about its exact value. A future\nrefactor will rebind this `def` to the Hecke-port output\nonce the categorical pipeline returns a Lean-typed real;\nevery downstream proof continues to type-check unchanged.\n\nUntil then, the literal acts as a *placeholder witness*\n(same role as the axiom, but with positivity provable). ","signatureChunk":0}]}